# Mint pilot — held back until the mint itself.
# Not secrecy: the structures are public-domain PubChem and the curation is
# published in data/. It's that token IDs stay volatile until a contract fixes
# them (a single data fix on 2026-07-31 renumbered 56 of 95), so publishing them
# early invites stale references. mint/ regenerates exactly from data/rows2.json
# + generators/build_mint.py, both tracked here, so nothing is lost by ignoring it
# and the git history still dates the curation.
# Publish at mint time, together with the contract address and tx hashes.
mint/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
